note: |
  BLIND-EVALUATION SNAPSHOT. NOT a publishable artifact and NOT a version of Ed-Fi.
  Purpose: measure the inference bridge against Ed-Fi's own authored CEDS crosswalk without
  letting the bridge see the answer. Two transformations, both mechanical:

  1. BLINDED. Every column whose name begins with 'CEDS' is present but EMPTY, in BOTH files
     (21 columns in the elements file, 6 in the descriptors file). This is a SOURCE-level blind:
     the answer never enters the parser, so nothing downstream can leak it. Blinding at the graph
     instead was tried first and found insufficient — the answer also rides in crossRefs, in
     cedsOriginalAnchorPropertyName, and would ride in any 'holdout' property added to stash it,
     because the evidence renderer prints EVERY scalar the source node carries
     (evidenceRenderer.js renders all keys except vector/embedding/searchText/stableId/_id/embedText).

  2. SUBSETTED to 98 property rows, deterministically: all 1,666 element rows sorted by
     (EdFiEntity, EdFiElementName), then every 17th taken. 69 entities are represented. No
     hand-picking, so the sample carries no selection bias toward easy or hard matches.
     The descriptors file is HEADER ONLY — this snapshot evaluates the PROPERTY tier.

  A partially-populated entity still forges a correct class node: the class name and description
  come from EdFiEntity/EdFiEntityDescription, which every row carries.

  The withheld answers live in dataStores/blindEval/propertyAnswerKey.json, read from snapshot 01.
